printf is a function which will print first argument as it is on the screen 
That first argument must be there in " ".
If we have multiple arguments should be seperated with comma.
If we have format specifier instead of printing it will map with the next argument.

eg: 
printf("Happy People");     //Happy People
printf("Happy","People");    //Happy
printf("Happy" "People");    //HappyPeople
printf(" " ");               //Compilation error 
printf(";");                //;
printf("%d",10);              //10
printf("%d%d",10,20);        //1020
printf("%f",1.2);            //1.2000000
printf(" "Happy " ");        //compilation error
printf("%d",5.7);            //garpage value - format speciifier is integer but we try to print float 
printf("%d","A");           //65
printf("%d %d %d",10,20);       //10 20 Gv
printf("my age is %d",20);      //my age is 20
printf("%d %d %d" ,"%d %d",10,20,30,40,50,60);      //Garpage value 10 20 



